      "title": "UK support for Falkland Islands 'unwavering' after Argentina restates claims, No 10 says",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn45jg3zlz4o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "The comments come as Argentinian president Javier Milei says the \"winds of change\" favoured his country's claim on the British overseas territory.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-09-04T11:54:51"
    },
    {
      "title": "Javier Milei: ‘winds of change’ support Argentina’s claim to Falkland Islands",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/president-javier-milei-winds-of-change-support-argentina-claim-to-falkland-islands",
      "description": "<p>President cites Trump’s suggestion that he might reconsider US stance on British sovereignty and threatens swifter sanctions on UK oil interests</p><p>President Javier Milei has said “winds of change” favourable to Argentina’s claim to the Falkland Islands are blowing around the world in a televised address, citing signs that <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/31/trump-uk-sovereignty-falkland-islands\">Donald Trump may reconsider the US position</a> on the islands’ sovereignty.</p><p>“Recently, President Trump declared that the US is re-evaluating its historic position in relation to the Malvinas,” he said, using the Argentinian name for the islands.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/president-javier-milei-winds-of-change-support-argentina-claim-to-falkland-islands\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T09:31:52"
    },
    {
      "title": "UK hits back at Argentinian Falklands claim and insists islands remain British",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/04/uk-ministers-hit-back-argentinian-falkland-islands-claim",
      "description": "<p>Ed Miliband says Britain’s position remains ‘unwavering’ in response to remarks by Argentina’s president</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/04/reform-uk-donations-nigel-farage-james-orr-dan-jukes-channel-4-investigation-conference-jordan-bardella-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>British ministers have hit back after the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/president-javier-milei-winds-of-change-support-argentina-claim-to-falkland-islands\">Argentinian president said</a> “winds of change” favourable to his country’s claim to the Falklands were “blowing around the world”.</p><p>The foreign secretary, Ed Miliband, said the UK would “resolutely uphold” the self-determination of the islands after the Argentinian president, Javier Milei, said his country needed to take them back.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/uk-news/2026/sep/04/uk-ministers-hit-back-argentinian-falkland-islands-claim\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T09:24:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Reform suspends two officials over donations sting as Farage admits their comments ‘don’t look good’ – UK politics live",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/04/reform-uk-donations-nigel-farage-james-orr-dan-jukes-channel-4-investigation-conference-jordan-bardella-latest-news-updates",
      "description": "<p>James Orr and Dan Jukes, aides to Nigel Farage, stepped down after an investigation by Channel 4 News</p><p>British ministers have hit back after the <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/president-javier-milei-winds-of-change-support-argentina-claim-to-falkland-islands\">Argentinian president said</a> “winds of change” favourable to his country’s claim to the Falklands were “blowing around the world”, <strong>Kiran Stacey</strong> reports.</p><p>The <strong>Electoral Commission</strong> has issued a statement this morning saying it is in touch with the police about the undercover investigation into Reform UK. In a statement, it said:</p><p>We are considering all relevant information, in line with our regulatory remit, and we are in touch with the Met police.</p><p>The Electoral Commission has not approved the donor vetting process for Reform, or any other party. Parties are responsible for ensuring their internal processes and controls are fit for purpose.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/04/reform-uk-donations-nigel-farage-james-orr-dan-jukes-channel-4-investigation-conference-jordan-bardella-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T15:12:22"
    },
    {
      "title": "Has Reform UK donations exposé caused a split in Nigel Farage’s party?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/04/reform-uk-donations-expose-nigel-farage",
      "description": "<p>Senior party figures do not appear united, but Farage may be more concerned about impact on performance in polls</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/04/reform-uk-donations-nigel-farage-james-orr-dan-jukes-channel-4-investigation-conference-jordan-bardella-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Midway through an event at Reform’s annual conference on Friday there was question for the audience: who was worried about a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/04/nigel-farage-aides-step-down-reform-uk-investigation-political-donation-rules-breach\">Channel 4 News exposé</a> of potential wrongdoing by party officials over donations? Almost no hands went up. The faithful might be sanguine. But make no mistake, Nigel Farage faces yet another problem.</p><p>Careful plans have been again upset. After months of answering – or primarily dodging – questions about his own finances, Farage had planned to use Reform UK’s biggest conference yet to make a blitz of policy announcements.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/04/reform-uk-donations-expose-nigel-farage\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-04T15:12:20"
    },
